# Slice 297 probe (CALLABLE-PLACE-NAMED-RECEPTION, a direct call): `gm(x: 300; y: 7)` -- the literal named x takes the context
# of the formal x of the callable the call selects, char: 300 is no char, the implicit `convert` before the body (25); a
# refusal at translation is the static check by the written signature.  `gm(x: 5; y: 300)`: 350.  Exit: 7, else the value
# seen (40 for another).
fn: gm (int: y; char: x) int
    return: (cast: (int) x) * 10 + y
end: gm
fn: call_wide () int
    ---
        int: got gm(x: 300; y: 7)
        return: got
        catch: convert ()
            return: 25
    ---
end: call_wide
fn: call_y () int
    ---
        int: got gm(x: 5; y: 300)
        return: got
        catch: convert ()
            return: 25
    ---
end: call_y
fn: run () int
    int: v call_wide()
    if: v != 25
        return: 40
    ---
    v: call_y()
    if: v != 350
        return: 41
    ---
    return: 7
end: run
int: code run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
